// Guarding the Yajna — Bala Kanda
// Source: Valmiki, Bala Kanda, sargas 27-30 (verify)
// Staged for the Ramlila stage, with the astra traced on stage and a scene after the fight.

>> scene ashram
>> cast vishvamitra at 0.66 face=left
>> cast rama:prince at 0.44
>> cast lakshmana:prince at 0.3
Morning. The sage is smiling, which is rare.
VISHVAMITRA: You did what I asked, and you took no joy in it. Sit facing east, Rama. I have weapons to give you.
>> together
>> pose rama kneel
>> pose vishvamitra raise
>> wait 0.5
>> sound bell
He speaks their names, and the astras come: shining figures standing in a ring around the prince, waiting to be called.
VISHVAMITRA: An astra is called by its sign. Draw it clean and it answers in full. Draw the sun.
>> astra sun
VISHVAMITRA: They are yours. Think of them, and they will come.
>> together
>> pose rama stand
>> pose vishvamitra stand
>> wait 0.4
>> scene ashram clear
>> prop altar altar at 0.72 state=0.6
>> together
>> enter vishvamitra from left to 0.82 in 2.6
>> enter rama:prince from left to 0.42 in 2.2
>> enter lakshmana:prince from left to 0.3 in 2
>> pose vishvamitra sit
>> light night
Siddhashrama. The sage takes a vow of silence. For six days and six nights he will not speak, and the fire must not go out.
>> face lakshmana right
LAKSHMANA: We will not sleep.
>> battle yajna
>> light full
>> pose vishvamitra raise
VISHVAMITRA: The rite is whole. You have kept your father's word and mine.
>> together
>> pose rama namaste
>> pose lakshmana namaste
>> wash
The sacrifice is complete.
Maricha, flung a hundred yojanas out to sea, lives. He will remember Rama.
-> END
